<!--Post: 15--><!--Time: 1085100228-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST15"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rosalita<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rosalita<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, May 20, 2004 - 5:43 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Does anyone know what happened to Bill Butterworth?  Is he still alive?  Seems like I remember reading somewhere that he had died in a car crash but I can&#39;t remember the source.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 15-->
<!--Post: 20--><!--Time: 1085152064-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST20"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Prairie_chicken<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Prairie_chicken<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, May 21, 2004 - 8:07 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->After the trial, he moved to Nebraska with his wife and children.  Their marriage did not last and wife and kids came back to Wichita, and I hear that they changed their surname to her maiden name.  She has remarried and no one seems to know of his whereabouts.  Maybe he did die in an accident.  Evidently it hasn&#39;t been confirmed.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 20-->
<!--Post: 24--><!--Time: 1085161927-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST24"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Laoise<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Laoise<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, May 21, 2004 - 10:52 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->There&#39;s an english professor who is writing a book about the butterworth case and has a yahoo group relating to the matter. I forget his last name but his first name is Paul. Anyway, someone recently asked the same question as to BB&#39;s whereabouts and he replied that he was almost certain he knew where bill was but wouldnt say... i took that to mean that bill is still alive somewhere and paul didnt feel it appropriate to release info as to where he was.  <BR>As to whether or not bill is btk... i personally dont think he is. if anything, he became a bit of a scapegoat for btk...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 24-->
<!--Post: 25--><!--Time: 1085163675-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST25"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sirfritz<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sirfritz<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, May 21, 2004 - 11:21 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Do you know where Paul teaches?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 25-->
<!--Post: 30--><!--Time: 1085181586-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST30"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lisa<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lisa<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, May 21, 2004 - 4:19 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->A friend of mine says that Bill Butterworth is his cousin and that he is afraid of him.  I remember everything they said about Bill Butterworth and when he mentioned that his cousin Bill was getting interrogated by the police, I asked him is it Bill Butterworth and he&#39;s like yeah.  I couldn&#39;t believe it, after all these people discussing him, this guy is my friend&#39;s cousin.  I don&#39;t know the whole situation of what happened there, if you would like I could find out where he is and if he is even a suspect anymore.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 30-->
<!--Post: 52--><!--Time: 1085275771-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST52"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Laoise<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Laoise<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, May 22, 2004 - 6:29 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->His name is Paul Fecteau and he&#39;s a professor at Washburn University in Topeka. <BR><a href="http://www.washburn.edu/faculty/pfecteau/" target=_top>http://www.washburn.edu/faculty/pfecteau/</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 52-->
<!--Post: 55--><!--Time: 1085301395-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST55"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ohenry<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ohenry<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, May 23, 2004 - 1:36 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Whether B.T.B. is BTK or not, I don&#39;t know. But there are some eerie coincidences that are rather hard to simply dismiss... <BR> <BR>Mr. Butterworth moved to Wichita in 1975 from California, but had visited several times since late 1973, early 1974. He then left Wichita in 1987 following his aquittal on three counts of first degree murder in the Fager case &#40;&#42;&#42;interesting time frame, no?&#42;&#42;&#41;. He was immediately employed by a company whose name I don&#39;t recall, but they made venetian blinds &#40;&#42;&#42;you might remember the role venetian blind cords played in this case&#42;&#42;&#41;. One of Wichita&#39;s most shocking trial outcomes EVER &#40;his aquittal&#41;, did not diminish the fact that was overwhelming evidence indicating guilt and undeniable similarities in BTK&#39;s m.o. and many areas of the Fager crime scene &#40;&#42;&#42;the use of heavy tape wrapped around the hands and feet of one of the girls &#60;&#60;bind&#62;&#62;; indications that the killer began drowning one of the victims, only to bring her back &#60;&#60;torture&#62;&#62;; and the brutal slaying of three people &#60;&#60;kill&#62;&#62;&#42;&#42;&#41; <BR> <BR>I never could confirm that he died in a car crash, and I find that unlikely. Has he returned to Wichita? Seventeen years have passed since he left; one can probably safely assume that his appearance has changed enough for him to feel safe.  <BR> <BR>Purplegrrl, where art thou? She is THE best source on Butterworth information. Hopefully she will comment on this thread. <BR> <BR>Again, I&#39;m not implying that this man is BTK, just that similarities should be noted. I AM implying that I strongly believe he got away with triple murder. Have a great one, -O&#39;Henry<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 55-->
<!--Post: 66--><!--Time: 1085365755-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST66"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lisa<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lisa<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, May 23, 2004 - 7:29 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Butterworth isn&#39;t dead, I know that for a fact from my friend, if anyone wants any information on him, I insist asking me and I will ask my friend who is this guys cousin, I&#39;m sure he wouldn&#39;t mind telling me about this guy.  He says Butterworth is insane and thinks he did it as well. <BR> <BR>Lisa<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 66-->
<!--Post: 68--><!--Time: 1085367923-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST68"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Marie<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Marie<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, May 23, 2004 - 8:05 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Does anyone remember when the Butterworth trial was going on, in the Eagle it stated that Fager owned a couple of the properties that BTK victims lived at?  However, it did not give names of victims.  Also Fager was being investigated by SRS for sexual abuse of the older girl &#40;Kelli??&#41;.   <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 68-->
<!--Post: 120--><!--Time: 1085786769-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST120"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:deltadawn194531@yahoo.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Sandy<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sandy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, May 28, 2004 - 4:26 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Ohenry,Can you tell us where in Calif. B.B. lived? Any pictures of him in the news papers at the time of his arrest ? I would like to draw a age progression picture of what he may look like today, and post it here.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
