<!--Post: 294--><!--Time: 1087282761-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST294"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Louise<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Louise<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, June 14, 2004 - 11:59 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Lisa,  I read with interest your entries that a friend of yours&#39; cousin is Bill Butterworth. Do you mean Paul Fecteau, the professor, is this friend and that his cousin is Bill Butterworth? If so, perhaps that is why he is writing the book about him. Or is your friend someone else? Would appreciate if you could clear up this question; also any other information you could get would certainly be helpful. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 294-->
<!--Post: 299--><!--Time: 1087444004-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST299"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sandy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sandy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, June 16, 2004 - 8:46 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Paul Fecteau was kind enough to send me some information about Bill Butterworth. I needed to know for sure, if B.B.spent any time in Calif. I was told B.B. was born in Philadelphia in 1954,but grew up in &#34;Calif.&#34;and went into the military. When he got out he went to Flordia,then around 1978 he moved to Wichita. I didn&#39;t ask him where B.B. was liveing now,but read on another site that B.B. is liveing very close to Wichita.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 299-->
<!--Post: 314--><!--Time: 1087889888-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST314"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Louise<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Louise<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, June 22, 2004 - 12:38 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Paul Fecteau, English professor at Washburn University, who coincidentally is writing a book about Bill Butterworth, believes that he knows where he is as he has sent letters to him, unanswered nevertheless! I researched Mr. Fecteau&#39;s other writings and found, oddly enough, a rather creepy story called Midnight Drive, about a man who lived in a remote area and had killed a woman. I couldn&#39;t seem to write the web site down right, but it&#39;s the 5th item under Paul Fecteau/Washburn University in Google. Hmmmh!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
