<!--Post: 325--><!--Time: 1088055912-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST325"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Louise<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Louise<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, June 23, 2004 - 10:45 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Wonder what happened to Lisa. She said she could get information from Bill Butterworth&#39;s cousin who also thinks he is guilty, and crazy as well. Still don&#39;t know if this cousin is Professor Paul Fecteau or not; his web site has been dead lately. I read that the police have interviewed Paul a number of times as they&#39;ve never seen anyone with such detailed, accurate information about the case. Hmmmh!? Plus he writes some pretty gory murder material &#40;Midnight Ride&#41;. After reading that I couldn&#39;t bring myself to read any more...it runs with blood and gore; and wouldn&#39;t it just be curious if some of the story details happen to match the true facts of the case?! Hmmmh again! How does he know so much?!! They say that blood is thicker than water.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 325-->
<!--Post: 347--><!--Time: 1088287222-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST347"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Matt<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Matt<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, June 26, 2004 - 3:00 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Bill Butterworth was also a suspect in another murder, previous to the Fager killings.  A sixteen year old female was killed at Crystal Lake, Northwest Wichita in the 80&#39;s; she was bound and strangled.  She belonged to a group of teens who thought they were a &#34;coven.&#34; Butterworth actually associated with this group a few times. After this girl was killed, two of the teens moved to Florida.  When Butterworth was arrested in Florida, he was within two miles of where these teens from Wichita lived.  This was not allowed to be introduced at the trial. Perhaps he was trying to tie up some &#34;loose&#34; ends.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 347-->
<!--Post: 352--><!--Time: 1088311396-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST352"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Louise<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Louise<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, June 26, 2004 - 9:43 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Interesting information about Bill Butterworth being a suspect prior to the Fagers, Matt. <BR> <BR>I still think there may be some clues in the writings of Paul Fecteau which are posted on the Internet. It is a given fact that the police have said he has extremely detailed and accurate information about the killings; therefore would it not follow that Professor Fecteau may possibly have posted some clues in his gruesome stories which he also posted on the Internet? If he indeed is a cousin of Butterworth he may be privy to much inside information. The stories were too creepy for me to read but one; however, there were more listed and other demonic stuff on his web site. I now have a totally different impression of what this BTK is truly like. Anyone read this stuff yet? <BR> <BR>And the final oddity is that Prof. Fecteau is writing a book with a number of chapters on this Bill Butterworth...hmmh! didn&#39;t someone else send in information about a book and its chapters?!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 352-->
<!--Post: 826--><!--Time: 1092984914-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST826"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Dbragel<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Dbragel<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->8-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, August 19, 2004 - 11:55 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->To: Matt <BR>Reply to: <BR>&#34;A sixteen year old female was killed at Crystal Lake, Northwest Wichita in the 80&#39;s; she was bound and strangled.&#34; <BR> <BR>Matt...I thought according to newspaper articles, it stated that Shannon Olson was &#34;bound and stabbed&#34;. <BR> <BR>Was she bound, strangled, AND stabbed? <BR>Also...if she was all three, do you know if she was strangled, but not to the point of death? <BR> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 826-->
<!--Post: 827--><!--Time: 1092986808-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST827"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Dbragel<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Dbragel<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->8-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, August 20, 2004 - 12:26 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->To: Sandy <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.beahoops.com/index.html" target=_top>http://www.beahoops.com/index.html</a> <BR> <BR>[Not sure if same person, but scroll down the page]<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 827-->
<!--Post: 1220--><!--Time: 1097786629-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1220"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nostone<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nostone<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, October 14, 2004 - 1:43 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I don&#39;t think anyone dumb enough to leave the scene of a murder and drive the stolen family car and remain with that vehicle could be clever enough to do the stuff BTK has done.  Don&#39;t get me wrong, I&#39;m not a BTK fan or anything.  I just don&#39;t think he&#39;s a moron either.  Which BB seems to be.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1220-->
<!--Post: 1431--><!--Time: 1101071358-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1431"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Oliver<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Oliver<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, November 21, 2004 - 1:09 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I wonder if the authorities have ever requested a sample of Butterworth&#39;s DNA?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1431-->
